      "writtenOn": "2021-01-27T21:32:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The question with the baseboard (or supplying FP_SENSOR to make) is whether we want to call the baseboard \"bloonchipper\". I think the answer is no. Bloonchipper means F412 + FPC1025. It\u0027s confusing to mention \"bloonchipper with ELANxyz sensor\".\n\nUsing the nucleo-f412 baseboard is also confusing because there are settings specific to the nucleo boards (but not the FPMCU) and we would have to override that in pineapple.\n\nSo I think I\u0027ll do the symlinks. Since we want a different board name + avoid code duplication, the symlinks seem reasonable to me even in the long run.",
      "parentUuid": "7eba63ae_01a68da0",
      "revId": "54c1474a0b1d0cac5b30c84d4295a76132cc5f4f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15b84e98_5be8775d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-27T21:58:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right now \"bloonchipper\" means F412 + FPC1025, but that\u0027s mostly artificial. We intentionally added a \"sensor select\" GPIO on the boards so that everything would be the same on the STM32F412 or STM32H743 board and we can determine what sensor we have attached: http://shortn/_T1nM7qVw9Q.\n\nThe piece that is missing is being able to either:\n\n1) build both sensor libraries into the same firmware (I think we have enough space in RW, but the symbol names in the vendor library might collide at the moment -- haven\u0027t tried).\n2) encode the sensor type into the firmware version (and name) so that we can determine which one to use. Something like \"bloonchipper-fpc\" and \"bloonchipper-elan\".",
      "parentUuid": "45491d98_9980e92b",
      "revId": "54c1474a0b1d0cac5b30c84d4295a76132cc5f4f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9936dd93_33e63bb9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
